        -: 1397:// Asynchronous method call events: these event are processed by wxEvtHandler
        -: 1398:// itself and result in a call to its Execute() method which simply calls the
        -: 1399:// specified method. The difference with a simple method call is that this is
        -: 1400:// done asynchronously, i.e. at some later time, instead of immediately when
        -: 1401:// the event object is constructed.
        -: 1402:
        -: 1403:// This is a base class used to process all method calls.
        -: 1404:class wxAsyncMethodCallEvent : public wxEvent
        -: 1405:{
        -: 1406:public:
        -: 1407:    wxAsyncMethodCallEvent(wxObject* object)
        -: 1408:        : wxEvent(wxID_ANY, wxEVT_ASYNC_METHOD_CALL)
